title: The Factory Gates
subtitle: Most workers are still at work.
view-if: crisis_march = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Factory Gates

In most of the country the factories are working. The strike call has been read and ignored. In some districts our comrades are asking the Zentrale for permission to close the gates themselves, with the unemployed, by force if need be.

- @unemployed: Send the unemployed to close the factories.
- @meetings: Hold factory meetings and let them vote.
- @strike_pay: Pay strike money to those who come out.

@unemployed
subtitle: The Left's line. It may close the gates. It will also set worker against worker.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 6; worker_support -= 4; unity -= 4; spd_relation -= 4; offensive_satisfaction += 4; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 6; lean_offensive += 1

Columns of unemployed men march to the gates at dawn. At some works they turn the shift back. At others the workers fight them with iron bars, and the photographs are in every newspaper by noon.

@meetings
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Spartacist way: the workers decide. It works where we are trusted.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.crisis_momentum += (Q.worker_support >= 25) ? 6 : 2;
Q.worker_support += 1;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Our factory cells call mass meetings and put the strike to the vote. Where the vote is won, the whole shift walks out together. Where it is lost, we accept it.

@strike_pay
subtitle: The Right's way. Costs 1 fund.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; crisis_momentum += 5; worker_support += 1; unionist_satisfaction += 3; lean_unionist += 1

The strike funds are opened. A worker who knows his family will eat is a worker who can stay out another week.
